WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.287
Production PostgreSQL supports REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY under specific conditions.

00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:09.277
An appropriate unique index is required.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:12.612
Concurrent refresh is an availability technique.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:18.777
It does not remove the need for a refresh policy, freshness metadata, or monitoring.

00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:25.522
A materialized view stores the query result physically, trading freshness for faster reads.

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:29.652
That makes refresh policy part of the data contract.

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:35.167
A dashboard should know whether the snapshot is five minutes old or one day old.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:40.294
Indexes can improve access, and concurrent refresh has additional requirements.
